## 6. Chart Column Configuration

Columns are `SheetRow[]` stored on `ChartConfig.inlineData`. Each column has `id`, `label`, `value`, `group`. Per-column color is derived from `style.colors[i % colors.length]` in `getChartData`, but `updateChartColumn` can set an explicit `color` on the row. `addChartColumn` appends a new row and extends the color list; `removeChartColumn` enforces a minimum of one column.

## 7. Wiring In a New Chart Type

To add, say, a `line` chart:

1. **Types** (`src/types/document.ts`): extend `ChartType`:
   ```ts
   export type ChartType = "bar-v" | "bar-h" | "pie" | "line";
   ```

2. **Component** (`src/components/charts/LineChartView.tsx`): create a new Recharts-based view accepting `{ data: ChartDataPoint[]; colors: string[]; showLabels: boolean }` (match the props contract used by `BarChartView`/`PieChartView`).

3. **Dispatch** (`src/components/charts/ChartCanvas.tsx`, ~lines 186-199): add a branch for `chart.type === "line"` rendering `<LineChartView ... />`.

4. **Toolbar buttons** (`ChartCanvas.tsx`, `CHART_BUTTONS` lines 15-39): add an entry with icon + label + type.

5. **Store** (`src/store/documentStore.ts`, `addChart` ~lines 392-439): add a title to the `titles: Record<ChartType, string>` map (this is a `Record`, so TypeScript will force it).

6. **UI entry points**:
   - `WelcomeScreen.tsx` — optionally add a "Start with Line Chart" quick action.
   - `SpreadsheetView.tsx` `createChartFromSelection` — widen the `type` union and add a submenu item.
   - `LibraryPanel.tsx` — add a menu item calling `addChart("line", sheet.id)`.

7. **StylePanel** (`src/components/shell/StylePanel.tsx`): update the per-type value label mapping (e.g. "Y" for line) and any type-specific controls.

8. **Optional**: if the new type needs different data semantics (e.g. multi-series), extend `ChartDataPoint` in `src/lib/charts/bindData.ts` and adjust `getChartData` mapping.

Because `ChartType` is used in `Record<ChartType, string>` in `addChart`, TypeScript will surface most missed spots at compile time.

