- `electron/main.js` — main process (window, IPC, engine spawn)
- `electron/preload.js` — preload bridge
- `renderer/` — UI (`index.html`, `app.js`, `styles.css`)

`package.json` still points `"main"` at that Electron entry and has `npm start` / `npm run dev` plus `electron-builder` pack scripts. The README calls it **dev-only** and not needed for the npm CLI. It is also **not** in the published package `files` list, and there is no `assets/` folder for icons, so it is source in the repo, not a finished installer.

There is **no Unreal app** in this folder: no `.uproject`, `.uplugin`, `.uasset`, Unreal C++, or even the word “Unreal” in the project files. Cursor’s Unreal MCP is a Cursor-side tool, not part of this repo.

I’ll strip the Electron desktop shell and every related script, dependency, and doc reference so this repo is CLI-only.
