## Architecture summary

**Model Studio** (v1.1.17) is a **local desktop Electron app** for project-based SFT and FrankenMoE. Training always runs as a **local Python subprocess** on the user’s machine (CUDA / Intel XPU / AMD ROCm / CPU). There is **no cloud/remote training path**.

```
renderer (vanilla HTML/JS)
    ↓ IPC via preload
electron/main.js (electron-store settings, spawns engine)
    ↓ JSON-RPC over stdin/stdout
engine (Node: modelstudio-engine.js)
    ↓ spawn(python, workers/*.py)
Python workers (train_sft, merge_moe, export, …)
```

| Layer | Tech | Key paths |
|--------|------|-----------|
| Frontend | Electron + vanilla `renderer/` (no React/Vue) | `c:\Users\Waylon Brown\Downloads\ModelStudio-App\renderer\` |
| Shell | Electron main + preload | `electron\main.js`, `electron\preload.js` |
| Backend / orchestrator | Node JSON-RPC engine | `engine\bin\modelstudio-engine.js`, `engine\lib\projects.js` |
| Training | Python (TRL `SFTTrainer`, PEFT, optional Unsloth) | `workers\train_sft.py` |
| Inference | llama.cpp / OpenAI-compatible local server | `engine\lib\inference_server.js`, `server\` |
| Persistence | `~/Downloads/ModelStudio` (or `~/ModelStudio`) + `electron-store` | projects under `{exportRoot}/projects/` |

