## Diagnosis: Project Rename

### Summary
The rename UI is present in source and in dist-v1.1.5, and the engine does persist name changes. The failure is a renderer focus/blur race: clicking Rename opens the input, then the button immediately steals focus, blur fires, and the edit commits the unchanged name — so it looks like naming is blocked.

## 1. Renderer rename UI (source)

HTML — rename controls exist (renderer/index.html:187-189):

```html
<div class="proj-title-row">
  <h2 id="proj-title" class="proj-title" title="Click to rename">Project</h2>
  <button class="btn ghost small-btn" id="btn-rename-project" type="button" title="Rename project">Rename</button>
```

JS flow — beginRenameProject swaps the <h2> for an <input>, blur saves (renderer/app.js:337-381):

```js
function beginRenameProject() {
  if (!state.project) return;
  const title = $('#proj-title');
  if (!title || title.tagName !== 'H2') return;
  // ... build input ...
  title.replaceWith(input);
  input.focus();
  input.select();
  // ...
  input.addEventListener('blur', () => finish(true));
}
```

Wiring at startup (renderer/app.js:1230-1231):

```js
$('#proj-title')?.addEventListener('click', beginRenameProject);
$('#btn-rename-project')?.addEventListener('click', beginRenameProject);
```

Save path — engine call is correct (renderer/app.js:320-334):

```js
async function renameProject(newName) {
  // ...
  if (name === state.project.name) return;   // silent no-op when unchanged
  const res = await modelstudio.engineCall('projects.update', { id: state.project.id, name });
```

## 2. dist-v1.1.5 packaging

Rename code IS included in the packaged app. Grepping app.asar found beginRenameProject, btn-rename-project, `input.addEventListener('blur', () => finish(true))`, and the proj-title-input CSS. This is not a stale-build issue.

## 3. Engine projects.update / name handling

Name updates work in engine/lib/projects.js:167-182:

```js
function updateProject(exportRoot, id, patch) {
  const cur = readProject(exportRoot, id);
  if (!cur) throw new Error(`Project not found: ${id}`);
  const next = defaultProject({ ...cur, ...patch, id: cur.id, createdAt: cur.createdAt });
  const nameChanged = Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(patch, 'name');
  const pathPatched = Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(patch, 'modelPath');
  if (nameChanged && !pathPatched) {
    next.modelPath = path.join(projectDir(exportRoot, id), 'output', slugify(next.name));
  } else {
    next.modelPath = resolveOutputPath(exportRoot, next);
  }
  return writeProject(exportRoot, next);
}
```

The engine does not reject renames; projects.update in modelstudio-engine.js (~line 653) passes the patch through.

Secondary engine issue (not the naming UI bug): renaming after training always rewrites modelPath to a new slug folder even if the model already exists at the old path. That can break "Open output" later, but the display name still saves.

## 4. Root cause: blur/focus race (primary)

What happens when the user clicks Rename:
1. beginRenameProject() runs (app.js:337).
2. The <h2 id="proj-title"> is replaced with a plain <input> with no id (app.js:342-347).
3. input.focus() runs (app.js:348).
4. The click handler returns; the button receives focus (default <button> behavior).
5. Input blurs -> finish(true) (app.js:380).
6. renameProject(input.value) runs with the original name.
7. app.js:327 `if (name === state.project.name) return` — silent no-op.
8. Input is removed; title shows the old name again.

User experience: the input flashes and disappears instantly — "won't let me name projects."

Clicking the <h2> title can sometimes work because no focusable element steals focus afterward, but the explicit Rename button hits the bug every time.

Related issues in the same code:
- Blur saves on any focus loss (app.js:380) — immediate commit with no chance to type.
- Input has no id="proj-title" during edit (app.js:342-347) — #proj-title is null while editing, so a Rename click is a no-op (app.js:340).
- Unchanged name is a silent no-op (app.js:327) — no feedback when the blur race commits the old name.
- renderProject only sets textContent on the H2 (app.js:180-183), so it does not destroy click handlers; "handlers lost after renderProject" is NOT the cause.

## 5. Create-project naming vs rename

Create uses a separate modal and works (renderer/app.js:383-394):

```js
async function createProject() {
  const name = $('#modal-name').value.trim();
  if (!name) return alert('Name your project.');
  const res = await modelstudio.engineCall('projects.create', { name, type });
```

Modal markup is normal (index.html:475) with no readonly/disabled on #modal-name. Typical flow: create with a name -> open project -> try to rename via the Rename button -> hits the blur race. The complaint reads as "can't name projects" even though create works.

## Exact fix (minimal) — all in renderer/app.js

Fix A — stop the Rename button from stealing focus (required). Replace line 1231 with:

```js
$('#btn-rename-project')?.addEventListener('mousedown', (e) => e.preventDefault());
$('#btn-rename-project')?.addEventListener('click', (e) => {
  e.preventDefault();
  beginRenameProject();
});
```

Fix B — defer blur so focus can settle (recommended). Replace line 380:

```js
input.addEventListener('blur', () => {
  setTimeout(() => { if (!done) finish(true); }, 0);
});
```

Fix C — capture the value before the DOM swap (recommended). In finish() (~lines 352-368):

```js
const savedValue = input.value;
// ... replaceWith(h2) ...
if (save) {
  try { await renameProject(savedValue); }
```

Fix D — give the input id="proj-title" during edit (optional hardening). After line 344 add `input.id = 'proj-title';` and update the guard at line 340 to `if (!title || title.tagName !== 'H2') return;` so renderProject's `tagName === 'H2'` check (line 181) stays safe.

## Secondary fix (engine, post-train rename)

In engine/lib/projects.js lines 177-178, avoid rewriting modelPath when a completed model already exists at the old path (or move/rename the output dir). This does not fix the UI naming bug but prevents broken output paths after rename.

## Rebuild note

After fixing renderer/app.js, rebuild so the next dist picks up the change in app.asar. The current v1.1.5 build has the buggy blur handler baked in.

Bottom line: rename was implemented and packaged, but `blur -> finish(true)` combined with the Rename button taking focus makes the editor close immediately with the unchanged name. Fix the focus race in renderer/app.js (Fix A + B); the engine path is already fine for persisting names.

