### 3. Shared expert YAML omits `positive_prompts` (breaks Qwen MoE path)
| | |
|---|---|
| **Severity** | **High** (for Qwen / Qwen-inferred arch) |
| **Where** | `workers/merge_moe.py` ~107–112 (`shared_experts` only has `source_model` + `residual_scale`) |
| **What's wrong** | MergeKit: DeepSeek forbids prompts on shared; **Qwen requires** them for `gate_mode: hidden`. No `architecture:` is set; inference + catalog (Qwen models) can select Qwen. |
| **Failure mode** | Always-on merges of Qwen experts fail MergeKit → scaffold (#2). Omitting prompts is intentional for DeepSeek-only; unsafe without pinning arch. |
| **Origin** | **New** (always-active / shared_experts). |

