## Hybrid placement / device mismatch

- **CPU embed + XPU batch device mismatch** — Trigger: `embed_tokens` / `embed_tokens_per_layer` kept on CPU after disk-stream offload; Trainer puts `input_ids` on XPU | Symptom: `RuntimeError` (“expected device xpu:0 but got cpu”), XPU op unsupported on CPU tensor, or extreme step latency | Severity: Critical | Pointer: `workers/train_speed.py` L458–472, L564–572; `workers/train_sft.py` L594–617

- **hf_device_map lost after PEFT wrap** — Trigger: `get_peft_model()` drops `_ms_hf_device_map`; re-stamp `except` swallows failure | Symptom: Trainer calls `model.to("xpu:0")`, duplicates ~5.25 GiB CPU embed into shared USM → OOM on step 0 | Severity: Critical | Pointer: `workers/train_sft.py` L592–617

- **hf_device_map fallback `{"": "xpu:0"}`** — Trigger: Re-stamp runs but `src` map missing/incomplete (no CPU module entries) | Symptom: Same as full `.to(xpu)` OOM despite “load succeeded” | Severity: Critical | Pointer: `workers/train_sft.py` L610–611

- **Per-module map key granularity wrong** — Trigger: CPU keys mapped via `key.rsplit(".", 1)[0]`; nested submodule paths may not match Accelerate expectations | Symptom: Some CPU tensors still moved to XPU, or wrong module placement | Severity: High | Pointer: `workers/train_speed.py` L415–418, L566–568

- **Tied `lm_head` on CPU, hidden states on XPU** — Trigger: `tie_weights()` shares `embed_tokens` (CPU) with `lm_head` | Symptom: Logits computed on CPU; cross-device copy each step; backward graph spans CPU↔XPU; NaNs or grad errors on some XPU builds | Severity: High | Pointer: `workers/train_speed.py` L503–547

- **Cross-device embedding every layer (Gemma-4)** — Trigger: `embed_tokens_per_layer` on CPU; per-layer embed in forward | Symptom: Training “works” but ~10–100× slower; UI looks hung; timeouts mistaken for crash | Severity: Medium | Pointer: `workers/train_speed.py` L448–472 (CPU keep path); load comments L276–281

