The catalog was stuck on **“Loading catalog…”** because when the Python backend wasn’t up, the API call threw and never fell back to the static model list.

**What I fixed:**
1. **`electron/main.js`** — `backend:proxy` returns a clean 503 when the backend isn’t ready, and catches fetch errors instead of hanging/crashing IPC.
2. **`renderer/src/api/client.js`** — `fetchModels` always falls back to the built-in catalog on failure.
3. **`SettingsView.jsx`** — Shows the static catalog immediately, then refreshes from the backend when available; shows an offline note if the backend never connects.

Restart the app (`npm start` or relaunch the portable exe). You should see all models in Settings right away, even with the orange backend banner.

