## App structure (marketing vs app)

Next.js App Router under `apps/web/src/app` with two route groups:

| Layout | Path | Role |
|--------|------|------|
| Root | `apps/web/src/app/layout.tsx` | Fonts, theme, toaster |
| Marketing | `apps/web/src/app/(marketing)/layout.tsx` | Public site + `MarketingNav` |
| App | `apps/web/src/app/(app)/layout.tsx` | Auth-gated studio: sidebar (desktop) + `MobileAppNav` |

`(app)` redirects unauthenticated users to `/login`. Middleware also gates `/home`, `/projects`, `/library`, `/account`, `/settings` by session cookie.

---

## Routes / pages

| Route | File |
|-------|------|
| `/` | `apps/web/src/app/(marketing)/page.tsx` |
| `/login` | `apps/web/src/app/(marketing)/login/page.tsx` |
| `/home` | `apps/web/src/app/(app)/home/page.tsx` |
| `/projects` | `apps/web/src/app/(app)/projects/page.tsx` |
| `/projects/[id]` | `apps/web/src/app/(app)/projects/[id]/page.tsx` |
| `/library` | `apps/web/src/app/(app)/library/page.tsx` |
