## 1. Project overview

**Cognitience WP** (`cognitience-wp` v1.2.2) is an Electron word processor positioned as “the VS Code of word processors”: rich editing, templates, multi-format export, themes, and a VS Code–style extension system (`.cogwp`).

| Layer | Tech |
|--------|------|
| Main / preload | TypeScript → CommonJS (`dist/`) |
| Renderer | Plain JS/HTML/CSS (`contenteditable` + `document.execCommand`) |
| Packaging | `electron-builder` (NSIS/portable Win, dmg/zip Mac, tar.gz Linux) |
| Runtime deps | `js-yaml`, `jszip`, `jsdom`, `adm-zip`, `marked`, `mammoth` |

**Main entry points**
- `C:\Users\Waylon Brown\dev\cognition-wp\package.json` → `"main": "dist/main/index.js"`
- `src/main/index.ts` — app bootstrap (WindowManager, ExtensionHost, PluginHost, IPC, menu)
- `src/preload/index.ts` — `contextBridge` API (`window.cognitience`)
- `src/renderer/index.html` + `renderer.js` — UI/editor
- Electron loads renderer via `WindowManager` → `dist/renderer/index.html` (assets copied by `scripts/copy-renderer-assets.js`)

Local folder is `cognition-wp`; npm/GitHub name is `cognitience-wp`.

---

